    "result_text": "All 279 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation cap on the `POST /api/owners` endpoint. When 20 owners already share the new owner's registration date (today), the 21st is rejected with **400 Bad Request**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's registration date; throws `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` once the count reaches 20. Grouping by registration date means the cap resets each day.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new checked exception, extends `Exception`) so it surfaces as an OfficeFloor escalation.\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java`** (new handler) \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing `OwnerAlreadyExists` handler pattern.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `ensureDailyLimit` step (under the `transaction` governance) after the uniqueness checks and before membership-number assignment.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp13Tests` acceptance test (create 20, expect the 21st to be `400`) passes, along with the full suite (279 tests green). Seed owners have a NULL registration date, so they don't count toward the daily total.",
